      "value": "@{667353ba8663454809d39116|full_name} hi, looks like this or something similar has just happened to me yesterday: i updated this avatar avtr_20234418-171e-4046-9e8b-3f2cc25ee26c (private) with an updated version of a fur shader and it crashed vrc repeatedly on 2 computers on load.\n\non the first computer the crash notified me of issues with something like audio drivers for ShareX (a program that i used long ago on that old PC) so i uninstalled those, and later it complained about xiph codecs, so i uninstalled those too. further crashes, and those on my main PC, didn't give me any additional info.\n\ni focused/reopened Unity and reuploaded the avatar (without any changes IIRC) under a new ID, avtr_ff814584-6a2b-437a-b606-9560710a0b2f (also private), and it works perfectly fine!\n\ncan you take a look at this case?\n\nalso, does that mean that the server processing isn't a read-only process? is there a good reason for that?\n\nPS: weirdly enough, the impostors of that broken avatar regenerated properly\n\nedit: this avatar no longer crashes me. yay?",
